From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: sin, cos and the rest stay precise under Direct3D 9
 (Wine patch 0925)

Direct3D 9 sets the x87 to 24-bit precision, and Wine's musl maths for
32-bit programs ran on the x87: sin(1e8) gave 0.0000004, and a large
argument overwrote the caller's stack, so a game could crash in sin()
after some minutes of play. Wine patch 0925 builds that maths for SSE2.
---
